A||N||5||TRL46202||What are the steps involved in dropping the cradle||||1||
Z||000000||TRL46202||04-26-2001||02:58 PM||||I have an 88GT and want to repair/replace the manifolds. What are the steps involved in doing this. remove the trunk side manifold first and the lower cradle to get to the front one?? Do I have to disconnect anything before lowering???<P>Any help would be great....<P>Thanks, Tom||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||04-26-2001||03:03 PM||||The distance you are going to drop it is not going to require disconnecting anything except two rubber hoses at the fire wall. At least if my memory serves me. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Formula88||04-26-2001||04:09 PM||||You shouldn't need to even take off any hoses.  I dropped the cradle till the engine was almost touching the rear trunk wall (loosened forward bolts only, pivoted it down on the rear) and all the lines, etc. had enough slack.  Just be careful nothing gets hung or pinched.||||reg||1
Z||000003||GT GT 87||04-26-2001||04:19 PM||||Formula 88     You're saying the front cradle bolts????????? Will it pivot down with the rear vertical bolts ??????  My front manifold has several bolts broken , is there enough room to get a small drill in there to drill and tap them out  ????  Steve<p>[This message has been edited by GT GT 87 (edited 04-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||04-26-2001||05:28 PM||||No, the description is a little vague - we removed the *rear* cradle bolts and it pivoted down, with the front cradle mounts acting as a hinge.<P>The back of the cradle lowered (almost) to the garage floor that way.||||reg||1
Z||000005||voyagerspe||04-27-2001||12:08 AM||||ok heres my 2 cents<P>Drop the cradle pull it out from under your car and do what you have to do.  Its not hard to drop the cradle and the time you waste trying to drill and tap holes while under, over, in and out of your engine compartment will excede the amount of time it takes to remove the entire cradle.  Also while the cradles out you can clean and detail the engine and trans(maybe some paint).<BR> ||||reg||1
